<HTML>
<HEAD>
   <TITLE>Help </TITLE>
   <META content="text/html; charset=iso-8859-1" http-equiv="Content-Type">
   <LINK href="helpStyle.css" rel="stylesheet" title="WebEnabled" type="text/css">
</HEAD>
<BODY>
   <TABLE border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" width="100%">
      <!-- Begin logos row - middle logo is instrument specific -->
      <TR bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
         <TD bgcolor="#FFFFFF" height="60" valign="MIDDLE" width="230">
            <IMG alt="Agilent" border="0" height="60" src="../image/agilent.gif" width="230">
         </TD>
         <TD bgcolor="#336699" class="blue" height="60" valign="top">
            <IMG alt="" src="../image/instrumentBanner.gif"></TD>
      </TR>
      <!-- End logos row -->
      <TR>
         <TD bgcolor="#336699" class="blue" colspan="2">
            <IMG alt="" height="2" src="../image/filltrans.gif"></TD>
      </TR>
   </TABLE>
   <H1>
      Modify Network Configuration Help</H1>
   <P>
      The <B>Modify Network Configuration </B>page lets you view and modify the network settings
      of the
      <%=sModel%>
      &nbsp;oscilloscope. The web page that appears when the "Configure Network" navigation
      tab is clicked is the Current Configuration page. If you wish to modify a setting,
      you must click the &quot;Modify Configuration&quot; button.
   </P>
   <P>
      These settings configure the instrument to operate in your specific network environment.
      Changes you make to configuration parameters are not effective until the "Apply
      Changes" button is clicked. The "Undo Changes" button will undo any changes made
      prior to clicking the "Apply Changes" button or pressing the "Enter" key.
   </P>
   <P>
      IP Settings may be configured using the following:
      <UL>
         <LI>Automatic
            <P>
               This parameter allows Automatic network configuration (via DHCP
            and AutoIP) to be enabled or disabled. When disabled (OFF),
            network configuration parameters must be entered manually.
            </P>
            <P>
               Factory default: ON
            </P>
      <p><B>If Automatic network configuration is ON, the values for the following three parameters are
         automatically determined. If Automatic network configuration is OFF
     then the following three parameter values can be modified. </B></p>
         </ul>
         <p>IP Settings to use in non automatic mode:</p>
         <ul>
            <LI>IP Address
               <P>
                  This value is the Internet Protocol (IP) address of the instrument. An IP address
                  is required for all IP and TCP/IP communications with the instrument. An IP Address
                  is 4 decimal numbers separated by periods. Each decimal number ranges from 0 through
                  255.
               </P>
               <P>
                  Factory default: 169.254.254.254
               </P>
            </LI>
            <LI>Subnet Mask
               <P>
                  This value is used to enable the
                  <%=sModel%>
                  &nbsp;to determine if a client IP address is on the same local subnet. When a client IP
                  address is on a different subnet, all packets must be sent to the Default Gateway.
               </P>
               <P>
                  A value of 0.0.0.0 or 255.255.255.255 indicates that no subnetting is to be done.
               </P>
               <P>
                  Factory default: 255.255.248.0
               </P>
            </LI>
            <LI>Default Gateway
               <P>
                  This value is the IP Address of the default subnet gateway that allows the instrument
                  to communicate with systems that are not on the local subnet. This is the default
                  subnet gateway where packets are sent which are destined for a device not on the
                  local subnet, as determined by the subnet mask setting. A value of 0.0.0.0 indicates
                  that no subnetting is to be done.
                  <BR>
               </P>
               <P>
                  Factory default: 169.254.254.254</P>
            </LI>
            </ul>
            <p>Name service settings:</p>
            <ul>
            <LI>Hostname<P>
                  If Dynamic DNS is available on your network, the Hostname parameter
              is registered with the Dynamic DNS service at power-on. If left blank, the
              hostname is set to a factory default value.
               </P>
               <P>
                  A Hostname must start with a letter and may contain upper and lower case letters,
                  numbers and dashes(-).
               </P>
               <P>
                  Maximum length: 15 characters.</P>
            </LI>
            <LI>DNS Server
               <P>
                  This value is the address of the Domain Name System (DNS) server. DNS is an internet
                  service that translates domain names into IP addresses. The instrument uses this
                  server to determine and display its hostname.
               </P>
               <P>
                  If DHCP and Dynamic DNS is available on your network, the DNS server parameter is not
                  needed as the DHCP server will assign one or more DNS servers. If a value is entered
                  for this field, then the entered value will be used and the server(s) returned by DHCP
                  will not be used. If no DHCP is disabled, the DNS server parameter is needed for the
                  instrument to be able to find and display its hostname.
               </P>
               <P>
                  Factory default: 0.0.0.0 (no DNS server)
               </P>
            </LI>
            <LI>Multicast DNS
               <P>
                  Enables or disables Multicast DNS. This lets the oscilloscope
              use Multicast DNS for name resolution on small networks
              without a conventional DNS server.
               </P>
               <P>
                  Factory default: ON</P>
            </LI>
            </ul>
            <p>Other settings:</p>
            <ul>
            <LI>Description
               <P>
                  This is the oscilloscope description.
               </P>
               <P>
                  Factory default:  Oscilloscope model and serial number
               </P>
            </LI>
      <LI>Password
               <P>
                  Whenever you connect the oscilloscope to a LAN, it is good
              practice to set a password. The password prevents someone from
              remotely accessing the oscilloscope via a Web browser and
              changing parameters. Remote users can still view the Welcome
              screen, view network status, etc., but they cannot operate the
              instrument or change its setup without the password.
               </P>
               <P>
                  Factory default: no password
               </P>
            </LI>
      <LI>GPIB Address
               <P>
                  This parameter configures the GPIB bus Address. Every device on the GPIB bus must
                  have a unique address. This address is used when transfers are made on the GPIB
                  bus.
               </P>
               <P>
                  Allowed values: 0 - 30. Factory default: 7
               </P>
            </LI>
         </UL>
</BODY>
</HTML>
